    {
      "dom_id": "question-147064",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "The ratio of sheep to goats in Manuel's herd is $3:1.$\nIf Manuel has $30$ sheep, how many animals are in the herd in total?",
      "worked_solution": "We start with the ratio $3:1$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of sheep, and the denominator represents the number of goats.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $30$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $10:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 10}{1\\times 10}=\\frac{30}{10}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Manuel has $30$ sheep and $10$ goats. So, the total number of animals in the herd is \n\n$$\n30+10=40.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
